IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-art02-making: Article 2 (Making of Jersey Legislation) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
--
-- The two deposited texts of Article 2(1) differ in sub-paragraph (b) only:
--   the text of 28 September 2021 (to 10 January 2024):  "by being sanctioned by order of Her Majesty in Council"  (src:l_8_2021_20240110:34)
--   the text of 11 January 2024 (to current):            "by being sanctioned by Order in Council"               (src:34)
-- so Article 2(1) has one function per text, each quoting its own text.
-- The facts are the same in both and so is the answer, which the tests show; the text a question is answered under is chosen by the date, in je21-seat-1-making-and-commencement.l4.
-- Nothing in the Law says the 2024 change altered the operation of the Law; NOTES.md section 5 says what the endnotes say and no more.
--
-- Forks registered here: L4 (the day a Law was made, when its three steps fall on different days) and L8 (whether Article 2(2) still needs adoption).

§ `Article 2 -- Making of Jersey Legislation`

§§ `2(1) A Law is made by three steps`

-- All three steps have to be done: they are joined by "and".
-- This is the text of 28 September 2021 to 10 January 2024.
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by order of Her Majesty in Council; and
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1), text of 28 September 2021 (src:l_8_2021_20240110:32-35)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` steps MEANS
        isJust (steps's `it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)
    AND isJust (steps's `it was sanctioned by Order in Council on`)
    AND isJust (steps's `it was registered in the Royal Court on`)

-- This is the text of 11 January 2024 to current.
-- src:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by Order in Council; and
-- src:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.[2]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1), text of 11 January 2024 (src:32-35)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` steps MEANS
        isJust (steps's `it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)
    AND isJust (steps's `it was sanctioned by Order in Council on`)
    AND isJust (steps's `it was registered in the Royal Court on`)

§§ `2(2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States`

-- Article 2(2) excuses steps (b) and (c) for a taxation draft that an Act of the States has declared to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019.
-- It does not mention step (a), and that Article 12(1) is not among the sources: fork L8.
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(2) (src:36)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
      reading IS A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` steps reading MEANS
    IF NOT steps's `it is a taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER reading
         WHEN `the declaration by Act of the States is all that Article 2(2) requires` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the taxation draft must also have been adopted by the States Assembly, which Article 2(2) does not excuse`
             THEN isJust (steps's `it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)

§§ `2(1), 2(2) and 2(4) Whether, and on what day, a Law has been made`

-- Has the Law been made?
-- By the three steps of Article 2(1), or by Article 2(2) for a taxation draft.
-- The text of 28 September 2021:
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by order of Her Majesty in Council; and
-- src:l_8_2021_20240110:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1) and (2), text of 28 September 2021 (src:l_8_2021_20240110:32-35, src:36)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
      reading IS A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` steps reading MEANS
        `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` steps
    OR  `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` steps reading

-- The text of 11 January 2024:
-- src:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by Order in Council; and
-- src:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.[2]
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1) and (2), text of 11 January 2024 (src:32-36)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
      reading IS A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` steps reading MEANS
        `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` steps
    OR  `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` steps reading

-- On what day was the Law made?
-- Article 2(4): "Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be", and for a Law the step that names registration is (1)(c).
-- With all three steps done the day is the day of registration, which is the later of the three when they happen in the order of Article 2(1).
-- When they do not (the Law was registered before it was sanctioned, say) the words allow another reading, L4: the day the last of the three steps was done.
-- With a step missing and no deeming, the Law has not been made and there is no day: NOTHING, the source's own absent case.
-- With a step missing and Article 2(2)'s deeming, the Law is treated as made and the Law does not say on what day: a refusal.
-- src:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by Order in Council; and
-- src:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.[2]
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1), (2) and (4) (src:32-36, src:42)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
      `the reading of the day a Law was made` IS A `Reading L4 of the day on which a Law was made`
      `the reading of Article 2(2)` IS A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` steps `the reading of the day a Law was made` `the reading of Article 2(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER steps's `it was adopted by the States Assembly on`
    WHEN JUST adopted
        THEN CONSIDER steps's `it was sanctioned by Order in Council on`
            WHEN JUST sanctioned
                THEN CONSIDER steps's `it was registered in the Royal Court on`
                    WHEN JUST registered
                        THEN JUST (`Article 2(4): the day of making once the three steps are done` adopted sanctioned registered `the reading of the day a Law was made`)
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no day if the Law has not been made` steps `the reading of Article 2(2)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `no day if the Law has not been made` steps `the reading of Article 2(2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no day if the Law has not been made` steps `the reading of Article 2(2)`

-- The day, once all three steps are done: the day of registration, or the latest of the three days on the other reading (L4).
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(4) (src:42)
GIVEN adopted IS A DATE
      sanctioned IS A DATE
      registered IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading L4 of the day on which a Law was made`
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 2(4): the day of making once the three steps are done` adopted sanctioned registered reading MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `the day it was registered, by Article 2(4)` THEN registered
    WHEN `the latest of the days on which the three steps of Article 2(1) were done`
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF adopted AT LEAST sanctioned AND adopted AT LEAST registered THEN adopted
                IF sanctioned AT LEAST registered THEN sanctioned
                OTHERWISE registered

-- What a Law that is missing a step has for a day: nothing, unless Article 2(2) treats it as made, and then the Law does not say.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(2) and (4) (src:36, src:42)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law`
      reading IS A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`no day if the Law has not been made` steps reading MEANS
    IF `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` steps reading
    THEN REFUSE "Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft as made without the steps of Article 2(1)(b) and (c) and does not say on what day it was made"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `2(3) and 2(4) Subordinate legislation`

-- Jersey subordinate legislation is made by adoption (Regulations, Triennial Regulations, an Act that is Jersey legislation: the proposition containing them is adopted by the States Assembly)
-- or by signature (anything else: signed by the person responsible, or, if made by a body, by a person acting in accordance with its procedural requirements).
-- src:37 | (3) Jersey subordinate legislation is made –
-- src:38 | (a) in the case of Regulations (including Triennial Regulations) or an Act that is Jersey legislation, by the proposition containing the Regulations or Act being adopted by the States Assembly; or
-- src:39 | (b) in the case of any other Jersey subordinate legislation, by being signed by –
-- src:40 | (i) the person responsible for making it, or
-- src:41 | (ii) if made by a body, a person acting in accordance with any procedural requirements of the body.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(3) (src:37-41)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making subordinate legislation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` steps MEANS
    CONSIDER steps's `its form`
    WHEN `a Law` THEN REFUSE "Article 2(3) is about Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is made under Article 2(1)"
    WHEN `UK extended legislation` THEN REFUSE "Article 2(3) is about Jersey subordinate legislation, and UK extended legislation is not made under this Law"
    WHEN `Regulations` THEN isJust (steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)
    WHEN `Triennial Regulations` THEN isJust (steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)
    WHEN `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` THEN isJust (steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`)
    WHEN `an Order`
        THEN     isJust (steps's `it was signed on`)
             AND (   steps's `it was signed by the person responsible for making it`
                  OR (    steps's `it was made by a body`
                      AND steps's `it was signed by a person acting in accordance with the procedural requirements of the body`))
    WHEN `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey`
        THEN     isJust (steps's `it was signed on`)
             AND (   steps's `it was signed by the person responsible for making it`
                  OR (    steps's `it was made by a body`
                      AND steps's `it was signed by a person acting in accordance with the procedural requirements of the body`))

-- Article 2(4): the day the subordinate legislation was made is the day it was adopted or signed, as the case may be.
-- Not yet adopted or signed as the Law requires: not made, so no day.
-- src:37 | (3) Jersey subordinate legislation is made –
-- src:38 | (a) in the case of Regulations (including Triennial Regulations) or an Act that is Jersey legislation, by the proposition containing the Regulations or Act being adopted by the States Assembly; or
-- src:39 | (b) in the case of any other Jersey subordinate legislation, by being signed by –
-- src:40 | (i) the person responsible for making it, or
-- src:41 | (ii) if made by a body, a person acting in accordance with any procedural requirements of the body.
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(3) and (4) (src:37-41, src:42)
GIVEN steps IS A `Steps toward making subordinate legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` steps MEANS
    IF `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` steps
    THEN CONSIDER steps's `its form`
         WHEN `a Law` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `UK extended legislation` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `Regulations` THEN steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`
         WHEN `Triennial Regulations` THEN steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`
         WHEN `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` THEN steps's `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on`
         WHEN `an Order` THEN steps's `it was signed on`
         WHEN `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` THEN steps's `it was signed on`
    ELSE NOTHING


§§ `Legislation made by the States (a gloss that Articles 7(2), 9(6)(b) and 11(3) need)`

-- Articles 7(2), 9(6)(b) and 11(3) speak of legislation "not made by the States", and the Law does not say what that is: fork L5.
-- On the reading taken, the legislation the States makes is what Article 2 says is made by the States Assembly's adoption:
-- a Law (2(1)(a)), and Regulations, Triennial Regulations and Acts (2(3)(a)).
-- Orders and other instruments are signed (2(3)(b)); UK extended legislation is not made in Jersey at all.
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:38 | (a) in the case of Regulations (including Triennial Regulations) or an Act that is Jersey legislation, by the proposition containing the Regulations or Act being adopted by the States Assembly; or
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) (src:33, src:38)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of legislation`
      reading IS A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` form reading MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`
        THEN CONSIDER form
            WHEN `a Law` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Regulations` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Triennial Regulations` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an Order` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `UK extended legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `made by the States means a Law only`
        THEN CONSIDER form
            WHEN `a Law` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
